meta {
  name: The scheme comes from the path
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/period-schemes/{{schemeId}}/periods
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Period 4",
    "code": "P4",
    "sequence": 4,
    "period_scheme_id": "{{schemeId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 400
}

docs {
  400, not 422, and the distinction is worth knowing. The body shape for a
  period has no period_scheme_id field at all, so the JSON decoder rejects it
  as an unknown field before the handler's own "taken from the path" check can
  answer 422. The same is true of bell_schedule_id on a bell schedule period.
  Where the field does exist in the shape - timetable_id on a slot, or
  calendar_day_id on a day schedule - the refusal is 422 instead. Either way
  the near miss fails loudly rather than writing the row under a different
  parent than the URL named.
}
